@peter-woodz Yes, search for Jazz and look specifically for attribution to a jazz musician and a place/time of performance/recording. Music that lists a distributor/copyright holder/recording label tends to be human made. For indie music, look for production credits like producer, sound engineer, etc. Also look for a non-generic song title. Real musician's don't call their work "Jazz Noir", just like book authors don't call theirs "words".

AI doesn't yet add that kind of "realism".

You can use my extension for Chrome to tell slop from real ("Deslop This!")
